<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<ValidationRule xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        🔴 THIS RULE REVERSES A RECORDED PRIOR USER DECISION. HIGHEST-RISK CHANGE IN THIS
        TRANCHE (agent-output/design-requirements.md §2 ITEM 1, §0.5 Q1, §8 RESIDUAL-10).
        Read this comment in full before touching this rule or the No_Backward_Stage_Movement
        rule it interacts with.

        1. THE 2026-08-30 DECISION. On 2026-08-30 the user was shown the full consequence of
           blocking Dead/Pass from Closed Won - that Closed Won would become inescapable in
           the app, with no bypass permission and no self-service recovery route - and,
           after that consequence was stated, REAFFIRMED the decision to build it anyway.
           See design-requirements.md §0.5 Q1: "YES - BUILD IT. User overrides the recorded
           invariant, with no replacement recovery route." This is not an oversight of the
           prior decision below; it is a deliberate, informed override of it, made on this
           date.

        2. THE SUPERSEDED INVARIANT, QUOTED VERBATIM, AND WHERE IT LIVES. The rule this file
           sits beside - objects/Opportunity/validationRules/
           No_Backward_Stage_Movement.validationRule-meta.xml - records in its own header
           comment "the user-required invariant that Dead/Pass stay reachable from every
           stage" and names the Closed Won -> Dead/Pass -> earlier-stage round trip as
           "the actual recovery procedure for a mistakenly advanced deal." That invariant is
           recorded THERE, dated to an earlier decision, and this file is what supersedes it
           for the Closed Won case specifically. No_Backward_Stage_Movement's own header has
           been amended in the same change as this file to retract the parts that are now
           false for Closed Won - see its comment for the retraction.

        3. CLOSED WON NOW HAS NO IN-APP EXIT. Every other route out of Closed Won was already
           closed before this file existed: ranks 1-7 are blocked as backward moves by
           No_Backward_Stage_Movement's rank map (Closed Won is rank 8, the highest), that
           rule's CARVE-OUT 2 (the Initiate Underwriting checkbox) explicitly excludes Closed
           Won as of its own 2026-08-04 amendment, and D4 rejected a bypass admin permission
           for backward moves generally. This rule closes the one route that remained. A deal
           that reaches Closed Won by mistake now REQUIRES AN ADMIN DATA FIX (e.g. a direct
           data update outside normal validation, or a temporary rule deactivation performed
           deliberately and reverted) - there is no button, checkbox or permission a user can
           be granted to reverse it. See design-requirements.md §5 P8: brief the team on this
           before go-live.

        4. NO BYPASS CUSTOM PERMISSION WAS ADDED. Do not add one to "fix" the dead end this
           rule creates - that would re-open D4, which the user explicitly rejected at the
           original design gate ("the block is absolute for users"). If a bypass is ever
           wanted, it needs its own decision gate, not a quiet addition here.

        5. A READER OF ONLY No_Backward_Stage_Movement'S HEADER WILL BE MISLED. That file's
           comment was written before this decision and, prior to this change's amendment of
           it, described Dead/Pass as reachable from Closed Won and named the round trip as
           the working recovery procedure. Anyone who reads only that file and not this one
           will reach the wrong conclusion about how to recover a mistakenly Closed Won deal.
           THIS FILE IS THE CURRENT DECISION. Point future readers here.

        MECHANICS: PRIORVALUE(StageName)-keyed, so this rule is transition-only and
        self-limiting by construction, the same stickiness property No_Backward_Stage_Movement's
        "CARVE-OUT 1 STICKINESS CHECK" documents for its own carve-out. An existing Dead/Pass
        record whose prior stage happened to be Closed Won is NOT affected retroactively - it
        is not changing StageName, so ISCHANGED is false and this rule cannot fire on it (see
        design-requirements.md §6.3(i)). The rule only blocks the SAVE that performs the
        Closed Won -> Dead/Pass transition itself. TEXT(StageName) is not used here (unlike
        No_Backward_Stage_Movement) because both sides of the comparison are single, known
        picklist values, not a CASE() rank lookup - ISPICKVAL() is the correct, and this org's
        documented, form for that.
    -->
    <fullName>Dead_Pass_Not_Allowed_From_Closed_Won</fullName>
    <active>true</active>
    <description>Blocks moving a Closed Won deal to Dead/Pass. Reverses a prior invariant (Dead/Pass reachable from every stage) per the 2026-08-30 decision - see the XML comment. No bypass permission exists; a wrongly Closed Won deal needs an admin data fix.</description>
    <errorConditionFormula>AND(
    ISCHANGED(StageName),
    ISPICKVAL(PRIORVALUE(StageName), &apos;Closed Won&apos;),
    ISPICKVAL(StageName, &apos;Dead/Pass&apos;)
)</errorConditionFormula>
    <errorDisplayField>StageName</errorDisplayField>
    <errorMessage>A Closed Won deal cannot be moved to Dead/Pass. Contact your administrator.</errorMessage>
</ValidationRule>
